On 25/05/2016 05:04, Timothy Lawrence wrote:
>
> Yes, but "za'o" can't be used in Lojban for both that word /and/ its=20
> structural class because Lojban has only one definition per word.
>
>
> In particular, how is this answered in Lojban?
>
>
> ma selma'o zo za'o
>
>
> (I hope that's correct Lojban?)
>
>
> And what are the other word classes?
>

In order to talk about cmavo belonging to a particular selmaho in=20
Lojban, you can either:
=E2=80=A2 use {lo cmavo be lo se cmavo be zo za'o} (=3D "the cmavo of the s=
ame=20
selmaho as {za'o}), or {lo selma'o dunli be zo za'o} (=3D "the things=20
equal to {za'o} in their selmaho");
=E2=80=A2 or use the experimenetal cmavo {ma'oi}=20
<http://jbovlaste.lojban.org/dict/ma%27oi>, which belongs to the ZO=20
selmaho (thus, same grammatical behavior as {zo}):  {lo cmavo be ma'oi=20
za'o} =3D "the cmavo of selmaho ZAhO".

Here's a nice mindmap that classifies selmaho:
=E2=80=A2 https://mind42.com/mindmap/03d7fb74-986c-4418-bb14-2dfb86d21dbc

mi'e la .ilmen. mu'o

